[Music]  when i got the call from dc comics to  write batman the ongoing series it was  super surreal i've wanted to write  batman my whole life you know it's  definitely been a very big dream of mine  you know i i have a batman tattoo you  know it's it's always been something i  wanted to do  and i've gotten the opportunity to work  on batman a few times i've actually  gotten it right on on this batman series  since rebirth it was just something that  was really important to me and so when i  i got that call i couldn't wait to get  started on working you know and i'm  immediately diving into it thinking  about the world like that night i i went  and i watched the first batman movie the  1989 one just to kind of remind myself  of something  of you know why i love batman uh so it's  very very surreal but at the same time i  was just so excited to get to work like  just to dive right in and get to writing  if you've been reading batman recently  or haven't been reading batman recently  it was important to me that both those  things were taken care of here that i  honored what james had been doing before  in the book for the last two years but  then i also wanted to make sure that you  hadn't been reading it you could just  jump right into it  you know part of the story is that we're  coming out of fear state which is a big  batman event  and afterwards you know gotham has gone  through a bit of a change they've all  kind of survived this scarecrow attack  and so the city is sort of changing and  batman sees that and because of the  events of fierce state batman is  actually leaving gotham for a bit and so  it gives us kind of a point of a news  story of a new case about maybe able to  leave gotham and you're able to pick it  up there so it allows you if you you're  coming into a new you get to have kind  of a new case and a new adventure  so keeping james's run in mind i think  one of the things that james really  brought to it was a lot of excitement  and he really brought a lot of new  things to it new characters new ideas  and new toys  and so i wanted to keep that running i  wanted to be able to still introduce new  characters like we're reducing his new  villain his name is this and we're gonna  go play with some new toys in the dcu  with batman but i also wanted to bring  bruce back into the main dc and start  having interact with different pieces of  dc we haven't seen in a while and then  for me you know one of the things with  james's run was it was and he just goes  back to james detective run too it's  like it's bruce plus a major supporting  cast the characters you had ghost maker  and punchline and harley and i want to  keep some of that running but i wanted  to get back into  bruce's head and and spend some time  with just batman and make sure  everything was through his point of view  and that was one of the ways i was going  to kind of depart from what he was doing  and take it on my my own spin was to  make it much more about just batman by  himself on this adventure  so with this new run like i said before  we're using this new villain uh their  name is abyss see for me it's always  been interesting of how batman uses the  darkness and shadows  to uh he uses them as a weapon against  people and so i started thinking what if  someone may figure out how to use that  against bruce  against batman and so that's where he  started developing abyss as a character  who also learns how to use the darkness  but also take the way batman uses it  learn from it and then turn it around  against him they were really fun  character and the way we're doing their  powers is stupid different so it's gonna  be really interesting and then jorge  molina who came in and got to do a new  design for this character and really  just kicked up with it  [Music]  with jorge he brings a kind of calm  horror and tension to it i've been a fan  of jorge's molinos for a long time i  actually recommended or a years ago  because jorge would do all these like  awesome pickups of batman online  and so i started like showing that work  to dc and being like this guy should do  batman something this guy should do  batman someday and sure enough the day  that they call me the batman they're  also like oh jorge's gonna do it so i'll  just kind of came together when i was  recommending him for that job it wasn't  for me it was i thought he would do a  really great job with that character  and sure enough i got lucky and he gets  a drop with me and so far like the  thoughtfulness that he puts into gotham  into the characters and to kind of this  energy of gotham and batman and he's  bringing so much to it  [Music]  you

